<title>FRANCE: MOROCCO NEGOTIATES 90,000 TONNES WHEAT PURCHASE.</title>
<headline>MOROCCO NEGOTIATES 90,000 TONNES WHEAT PURCHASE.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco was negotiating late on Tuesday in a bid to import 90,000 tonnes of soft wheat in September, European grain traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The tender is working now. The negotiations have started,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Tender offers had gone in for a deadline of 1530 GMT.</p>
<p>The tender is for 90,000 tonnes of wheat for September 7-15 arrival, broken down by port as follows.</p>
<p>    Casablanca	     30,000 tonnes</p>
<p>    Agadir		   30,000 tonnes</p>
<p>    Safi		     10,000 tonnes</p>
<p>    Tangier		  10,000 tonnes</p>
<p>    Nador		    10,000 tonnes</p>
</text>
